# Stage 6 — add Log Loss to saved CV results

Date: 2026-11-05 (Asia/Tehran)
Task: Additional Log Loss metric for Stage 6

## Scope and data boundary

- User requested binary cross-entropy/Log Loss on each outer validation fold,
  mean and sample standard deviation reporting, and model comparisons.
- Saved CatBoost OOF probabilities are used to calculate CatBoost fold Log
  Loss. Earlier Stage 2–4 files contain fold scores and selected settings but
  no prediction probabilities, so the six comparison estimators are refit on
  the same development outer folds using fixed or saved fold-specific settings
  solely to obtain probabilities for Log Loss.
- No CatBoost refit, parameter search, model selection, threshold selection,
  calibration, or held-out data access occurs in `--add-logloss` mode. AP
  remains the sole hyperparameter search objective.
- User explicitly requested changes to Stage 6 metric/comparison artifacts.
  The update mode writes only `fold_level_metrics.csv`, `target_summary.csv`,
  `aggregate_metrics.csv`, `model_comparison.csv`, `paired_comparison.csv`,
  `model_comparison.png`, and `stage6_report.md`. The existing OOF and tuning
  outputs are read-only in this mode.

## Implementation and review

- `.venv/bin/python -m py_compile mi_stage6_catboost.py` — passed.
- The first independent code review found that repeated runs could duplicate
  fold-level Log Loss summary columns. The implementation now drops all prior
  fold `log_loss`, `log_loss_mean`, and `log_loss_std` fields before rebuilding
  them. The second independent review passed and confirmed idempotent schema
  handling.
- Log Loss is computed after clipping probabilities to `[1e-15, 1-1e-15]`.
- Comparator refit warnings are stored in `paired_comparison.csv` and will be
  retained in this record after execution.

## Command and result

- `.venv/bin/python mi_stage6_catboost.py --add-logloss` — first attempt failed
  during comparator probability validation with a function-call signature
  mismatch (`TypeError`). It stopped before writing any Stage 6 outputs. The
  optional model-name argument was fixed and independently reviewed; the
  failed attempt remains visible in this record.
- Corrected `.venv/bin/python mi_stage6_catboost.py --add-logloss` — completed.
  It calculated CatBoost Log Loss from saved OOF probabilities and refit only
  the six existing comparators on the same outer development folds with saved
  settings. It did not fit CatBoost, retune models, or select anything by Log
  Loss. No fit/search/comparator-refit warnings were recorded.
- The first ad hoc validation command had a Python `SyntaxError` because of
  inline loop layout; it did not modify artifacts. The corrected
  development-only validation passed all checks.

## Validation

Independent output verification: PASS.

## Results and validation

- Log Loss mean ± sample SD for CatBoost: `DEATH_BINARY` 0.262 ± 0.027,
  `ZSN` 0.470 ± 0.025, `FIBR_PREDS` 0.317 ± 0.032.
- Best existing model mean Log Loss was Logistic Regression for `DEATH_BINARY`
  (0.295), Random Forest tuned for `ZSN` (0.465), and Random Forest
  preliminary for `FIBR_PREDS` (0.292). Lower is better; these are descriptive
  five-fold comparisons.
- Validated Log Loss in 15 CatBoost fold rows, 3 target summaries, 3 CatBoost
  aggregates, 21 seven-model comparison rows, and 90 paired rows. Recomputed
  CatBoost fold losses from saved OOF predictions matched within `1e-12`;
  means/sample SDs and paired differences/directions matched their source
  values.
- Independent reviewer confirmed all required outputs, AP-only search
  objective, no Log Loss selection, OOF development-ID/label alignment, zero
  warnings, and the updated four-panel plot. No held-out files were enumerated
  or accessed.
